    "show_share": true,
    "description": "All over the world the populations of bees and other key pollinators - the butterflies, hummingbirds and bats - are rapidly declining, largely because of human activities which include the use of chemical fertilisers and fertilisers. To raise awareness about these important organisms, the UN designated 20 May as  World Bee Day .",
